Interface contains abstract and public methods by default
interface Add{
  int addition(int a,int b);
} 

Interface also contains:
1. default method containing method body. These are introduced if after some days we need to add 1 more method , we have to change the all clases implementing them.
2. static method belongs to class, accessed by class not object.
3. private method belongs to interface only. Can be called by other default method body.

interface Animal {
    default void sound() {
        System.out.println("Some animal sound");
    }
}

interface Animal {
    static void info() {
        System.out.println("Animals are living beings.");
    }
} 

Functional interface containg 1 abstract method only.
